# Installed by asus-expertbook-linux (ish-firmware).
#
# The Intel Sensor Hub PCI driver (intel_ish_ipc) has system-sleep PM
# callbacks only, no runtime PM. When power/control is "auto" (powertop
# --auto-tune, TLP and similar set it for every PCI function), the PCI core
# runtime-suspends the ISH to D3hot, the sensor hub stops answering
# ("timeout waiting for response from ISHTP device") and the ambient light
# sensor disappears until the driver is reloaded. Keep it on.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x8086", ATTR{device}=="0xe445", ATTR{power/control}="on"
